T|                 FADE IN:                                                           
O|
Y|                 BEGINNING LOGO                                                     
N|                 The familiar logo WARNER BROS. PRESENTS COMES UP.                  
O|
N|                 After a beat, it is consumed by FIRE.                              
O|
N|                 It becomes AN AMERICAN FLAG, BURNING in the street.                
O|
S|          1      EXT. U.S. EMBASSY (TEHRAN) - MORNING                       1       
O|
N|                 Effigies of Jimmy Carter and the deposed Shah -- crowds            
N|                 chanting “Magbar Carter! Magbar Ahmrika!”  Fists in the            
N|                 air.                                                               
Y|                 SUPERIMPOSE:  TEHRAN - NOVEMBER 4, 1979                            
O|
N|                 YOUNG MEN AND WOMEN -- about 2/3 men and 1/3 women, some           
N|                 with flak jackets; about half the young women wear full            
N|                 chador.  Many wear plastic bibs with photographs of                
N|                 Ayatollah Khomeini.                                                
O|
N|                 PASTED TO ROOSEVELT GATE: photographs of STUDENTS who              
N|                 were killed under the deposed Shah of Iran’s regime.               
O|
N|                 Signs in English:  “U.S.A. RETURN THE SHAH” -- “JUSTICE            
N|                 FOR MURDER.”  A few IRANIAN POLICE attend -- more as               
N|                 bystanders than peacekeepers.                                      
N|                 A MAN frantically stabs an EFFIGY of the SHAH.                     
O|
N|                 An IRANIAN STUDENT films the scene with a Super 8 camera.          
O|
S|          2      EXT. EMBASSY GROUNDS - MORNING                             2       
O|
N|                 From INSIDE THE EMBASSY GATES we can hear the noise of             
N|                 the protest.  There are three primary buildings on                 
N|                 campus:  the CHANCERY, the embassy’s main building, THE            
N|                 AMBASSADOR’S RESIDENCE, and the CONSULATE.                         
N,G|                 We can see that the compound is securitized: sand-filled           
N|                 traps and steel bars on the windows of the consulate.              
O|
S|          3      INT. U.S. EMBASSY - CONSULATE OFFICE - MORNING             3       
O|
N,G|                 Now, we see the POV THROUGH those steel bars.                      
O|
N|                 Standing on a chair looking at the protest outside the             
N,I|                 gate, is BOB ANDERS, late 40s-50s, a consular officer.             
O|
O|                                                               CONTINUED          
O|
O|
